  {
   "slug": "what-we-are-reading-in-october",
   "title": "What we are reading in October",
   "date": "2026-10-15T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Five picture books our rooms loved this month, and simple ways to keep the story going at home.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Story time is one of the most important parts of our day. These are the books the children have asked for again and again this month.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A book about a hedgehog who is scared of the dark</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A counting book with very hungry ducks</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A story about a girl who builds a boat from boxes</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A wordless book about a rainy day</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A lift-the-flap book about who lives in the garden</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Keep the story going at home</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Ask what might happen next before you turn the page.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Let your child tell the story from the pictures.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Read the same book again; repetition is how little ones learn.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Every room has a cosy book corner, and the children choose the bedtime-style story we read together after lunch.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ls-callout\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group ls-callout\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our lending library is open at pick-up on Tuesdays and Thursdays. Borrow up to two books a week.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "categories": [
    "learning"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "books",
    "reading"
   ],
   "featured_media": "book-corner",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "healthy-snack-ideas-from-our-kitchen",
   "title": "Healthy snack ideas from our kitchen",
   "date": "2026-10-08T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Our cook shares the snacks that disappear fastest, and the trick that gets everyone trying something new.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our cook, Marisol, makes snacks for sixty children every day, and she has learned a thing or two about what actually gets eaten.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Her biggest tip: let children help. A child who has washed the carrots is far more likely to try one.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Marisol's top five</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Apple \"sunshine\" slices with a little yogurt dip</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Cucumber boats with cream cheese</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Banana and oat mini muffins</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Rainbow fruit skewers (soft fruit only for the little ones)</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Warm toast fingers with mashed avocado</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:snack-plate}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:snack-plate}}\" alt=\"A plate of fruit slices arranged like a smiling sun\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:snack-plate}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The fruit sun is always the first plate to empty.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ls-callout\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group ls-callout\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are a nut-free nursery. Please tell us about any allergies or dietary needs, and we will plan around them.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "categories": [
    "health"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "food",
    "families"
   ],
   "featured_media": "snack-plate",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "settling-in-tips-for-new-families",
   "title": "Settling in: tips for new families",
   "date": "2026-10-01T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Starting nursery is a big step for the whole family. Here is how our settling-in weeks work, and how you can help.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Starting nursery is a big change, for children and for grown-ups. Every child settles at their own pace, and our settling-in weeks are designed to go gently.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How settling-in works</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"ls-schedule\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list ls-schedule\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Visit 1</strong> <span>One hour together with you in the room</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Visit 2</strong> <span>You stay nearby while your child explores</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Visit 3</strong> <span>A short goodbye and one hour apart</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Week 2</strong> <span>Half days, then full days when ready</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How you can help</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Keep goodbyes short, warm and the same every day.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bring a comfort toy or a family photo.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Tell us about your child's routines, words and favourite songs.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Talk about nursery positively at home.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Some children wave goodbye on the first morning, others need a few weeks. Both are completely normal, and we will keep you updated with photos and messages during the day.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Most of all, ask us anything. Your key person is there for you as much as for your child.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "parents"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "settling-in",
    "families"
   ],
   "featured_media": "classroom",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Hannah W.",
     "content": "This helped so much. Our son now runs in every morning!",
     "date": "2026-10-02T17:45:00",
     "email": "hannah@example.com"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "garden-club-planting-bulbs-for-spring",
   "title": "Garden club: planting bulbs for spring",
   "date": "2026-09-24T14:00:00",
   "excerpt": "The Blossoms planted two hundred bulbs this week. Now comes the hardest part: waiting.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our oldest group, the Blossoms, spent this week with muddy hands and very serious faces, planting two hundred bulbs in the raised beds by the fence.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We talked about what a bulb needs (soil, water and patience), measured how deep to plant them with our fingers, and made labels so we remember what is where.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:garden-bulbs}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:garden-bulbs}}\" alt=\"Small hands planting bulbs in a raised garden bed\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:garden-bulbs}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What we planted</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Daffodils for the front bed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Crocuses in the grass by the gate</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Tulips in the Blossoms' own bed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We will check on them every week and draw what we see. Come and look in spring!</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "learning",
    "outdoors"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "garden",
    "nature"
   ],
   "featured_media": "garden-bulbs",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "pyjama-day-and-winter-book-drive",
   "title": "Pyjama day and our winter book drive",
   "date": "2026-09-17T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Come to nursery in your pyjamas on Friday 14 November and bring a book to give to a family who needs one.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our favourite cosy day of the year is coming! On Friday 14 November, children (and staff) can come to nursery in their pyjamas.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This year we are also collecting new and gently used picture books for the local family centre. Every book helps a child have a story at bedtime.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to join in</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wear pyjamas and bring warm clothes for outdoor play.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Bring a book for the donation box by the door.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Join us for a bedtime story session at 15:30.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:pullquote --><figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>Every book in the box is a bedtime story for another child.</p></blockquote></figure><!-- /wp:pullquote --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Last year families donated more than three hundred books, which filled the family centre shelves all winter. Let's try to beat it!</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "events"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "books",
    "families"
   ],
   "featured_media": "pyjama-moon",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "why-we-spend-so-much-time-outdoors",
   "title": "Why we spend so much time outdoors, in every weather",
   "date": "2026-09-10T11:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Mud, puddles and fresh air: why outdoor play is part of every day at Little Sprouts.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you have ever collected a very muddy child at pick-up, you already know: we go outside every day, rain or shine.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Outdoor play builds strong bodies, curious minds and brave hearts. Climbing, balancing and splashing help children learn what their bodies can do, and nature gives them endless things to wonder about.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What to pack</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Waterproof trousers and jacket</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wellies (labelled, please!)</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A spare set of clothes, including socks</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A sun hat in summer, a warm hat in winter</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:rain-boots}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:rain-boots}}\" alt=\"Red and yellow rain boots next to a puddle\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:rain-boots}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">A puddle is just a very small lake waiting to be explored.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ls-callout\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group ls-callout\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We have spare wellies and waterproofs for anyone who forgets. Just ask.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "categories": [
    "outdoors",
    "learning"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "nature",
    "play"
   ],
   "featured_media": "rain-boots",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "parent-evenings-this-term",
   "title": "Parent evenings this term: dates and what to expect",
   "date": "2026-09-03T16:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Fifteen minutes with your child's key person to talk about friends, play and what comes next.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Parent evenings are a chance to sit down with your child's key person and talk about how things are going: friendships, favourite activities and anything you would like us to know.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:table --><figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Room</th><th>Date</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Seedlings &amp; Sprouts</td><td>Tuesday 4 November</td><td>16:30 to 19:00</td></tr><tr><td>Saplings</td><td>Wednesday 5 November</td><td>16:30 to 19:00</td></tr><tr><td>Blossoms</td><td>Thursday 6 November</td><td>16:30 to 19:00</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We will share a short summary of your child's play and learning, a few photos, and the things they have told us they love doing most.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Booking a time</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You can book a time at reception or through the family app. Little ones are welcome to come along; we will have crayons and a quiet corner ready.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If none of the times work for you, tell us and we will find another moment.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "parents"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "families"
   ],
   "featured_media": "crayons",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  }
